  "name": "Glucose-6-Phosphate Dehydrogenase",
  "code": "G6PD",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul><li>Normal range: A normal G6PD test result indicates that the level of the enzyme in the blood is within the normal range. This means that the individual is not at risk of hemolysis caused by G6PD deficiency.</li><li>Low level: A low G6PD test result indicates that the level of the enzyme in the blood is lower than normal. This means that the individual may be at risk of hemolysis caused by G6PD deficiency if exposed to certain drugs or chemicals that can trigger hemolysis. The severity of the deficiency and the risk of hemolysis depend on the degree of enzyme deficiency and the specific drug or chemical exposure.</li></ul>",
